Apple today <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-introduces-the-new-14-inch-macbook-pro-with-m6/">announced</a> a refreshed 14-inch <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> featuring the M6 chip, upgraded connectivity specifications, and more.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe width="560" height="315" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/xWfNhWn88Bc?si=rQ6VkweZs-bsl7Kk" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div><br/>
The M6 chip in the &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; features a 12-core CPU with 2 super cores, 4 performance cores, and 6 efficiency cores, paired with a 12-core GPU. This is up from the M5 chip with a 10-core CPU with 4 super cores and 6 efficiency cores, paired with a 10-core GPU.<br/>
<br/>
<blockquote>M6 features an advanced 12-core CPU with the world's fastest CPU core, so everything from productivity tasks to more demanding pro workflows feels incredibly fast and responsive. The 12-core GPU delivers up to 30 percent faster graphics and up to 25 percent faster AI workloads when compared to M5, making the 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 a compelling value for users who need serious power.</blockquote><br/>
<br/>
The Neural Engine doubles from 16-cores to a dual 16-core Neural Engine system with 32 total cores. Memory bandwidth also increases from 153GB/s to 170GB/s, but only on models with 24GB and 32GB of memory.<br/>
<br/>
<blockquote>With additional Neural Accelerators in the GPU and a Dual 16-core Neural Engine, M6 turns MacBook Pro into an even more powerful platform for AI — from taking advantage of Siri AI and Apple Intelligence features across apps and macOS to running LLMs locally, all while preserving user privacy.</blockquote><br/>
<br/>
Alongside the M6 chip, the new 14-inch &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; now features support for Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6 connectivity via Apple's N1 wireless chip. It can also now drive dual external 4K displays at up to 165Hz, up from 144Hz.<br/>
<br/>
The 14-inch &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; continues to start with 1TB of storage. The previous model's 512GB configuration was <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/03/apple-m5-macbook-pro-storage-update/">dropped in March</a>.<br/>
<br/>
